<worksheet >
    <title>LSAI-2 Linear Independence</title>
  <introduction>
    <p>To earn an M on this outcome, complete all four problems. Complete problem 4 and two other problems to earn a P.</p>
  </introduction>  
  <page>
    <p>Suppose the augmented matrix associated with the matrix equation 
          <m>M\mathbf{x}=\mathbf{b}</m> has a reduced echelon form of 
          <md alignment="alignat" alignat-columns="6">
        <mrow>\begin{bmatrix} 1 &amp; 4 &amp; 0 &amp; -2 &amp; | &amp; 0\\ 0 &amp; 0 &amp; 1 &amp; 3 &amp; | &amp; 0\\ 0 &amp; 0 &amp; 0 &amp; 0 &amp; | &amp; 1\end{bmatrix}</mrow>
      </md></p>
    <exercise workspace="2in"><p>Write the general solution to the matrix equation in parametric vector form.</p></exercise>
      <exercise workspace="2in"><p>Is <m>\mathbf{b}</m> in the span of the columns of <m>M</m>? Why or why not?</p></exercise>
      <exercise workspace="2in"><p>Are the columns of <m>M</m> linearly independent? Why or why not?</p></exercise>
  </page>
  <page>
      <exercise><p>Let <md alignment="alignat" alignat-columns="1"><mrow>\mathbf{a}_1 = \begin{bmatrix} 1\\-2\\2 \end{bmatrix}, 
        \quad \mathbf{a}_2 = \begin{bmatrix} 2\\-3\\4 \end{bmatrix}, \quad \mathbf{a}_3 = \begin{bmatrix} 0\\4\\0 \end{bmatrix}, 
        \quad \mathbf{y} = \begin{bmatrix} -1\\5\\-2 \end{bmatrix}</mrow></md>. Determine if <m>\mathbf{y}</m> is a linear 
        combination of <m>\mathbf{a}_1</m>, <m>\mathbf{a}_2</m>, and <m>\mathbf{a}_3</m>. Support your answer.</p></exercise>
  </page>
</worksheet>